{"seq":11,"trial_id":"host-harness-pilot-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T19:08:32.569Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"b20ff58d699723dd91402b0b461bf98e425b744c2b2e4234e08f5bb8d131a253","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHOSTHA0001","text":"Two ticket numbers on Quarrendon Freight Lines turned up in Moss's notes:\n\n- **#4419**: Thea Ramaswell logged it for gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 during third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. Source: Moss's undated North cheat sheet (`dev/agent-notes/north-account-cheatsheet`).\n- **PD-4492**: Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025 for Pemberline Dock gatehouse kiosk alerts at the Eau Claire yard. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the shift cleared without manual intervention. Source: Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" note, 5 Oct 2025 (`dev/agent-notes/2025-10-05-north-sunday`). That note also has a 14 Oct maintenance-window follow-up on the Eau Claire kiosk logs.\n\nThe other two QFL notes (14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in) don't carry ticket numbers.\n\nCaveats: the brain search is keyword-only, so I can't promise this is every mention. These notes are Moss's briefings addressed to Ruth, so if they're not meant to be shared, check with her before quoting them in the weekly notes. I haven't written anything to a notes file. If you want, I can draft the two lines above for you to paste."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHOSTHA0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
